[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Range Filters & Inequality Constraints on Single Fields in Firebase Firestore"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"When querying data in Firebase Firestore, you often need to filter documents based on a range of values rather than an exact match. Firestore supports inequality constraints and range filters such as less than, greater than, and not-equal to help you build precise queries for your applications."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding Inequality Operators"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Firestore allows you to combine multiple filters to retrieve documents within a specific numerical, string, or timestamp range. The supported inequality operators include:"},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Less than (<): where('<field', '<', value)"},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Less than or equal to (<=): where('<field', '<=', value)"},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Greater than (>): where('<field', '>', value)"},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Greater than or equal to (>=): where('<field', '>=', value)"},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Not equal (!=): where('<field', '!=', value)"},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"Implementing a Single-Field Range Query"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"Suppose you have a collection of products and you want to retrieve all items priced between 10 and 50 dollars. You can chain multiple where clauses targeting the same field to create a range filter."},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"const { collection, query, where, getDocs } = require('firebase/firestore');

async function getProductsByPriceRange(db) {
  const productsRef = collection(db, 'products');
  const q = query(
    productsRef,
    where('price', '>=', 10),
    where('price', '<=', 50)
  );

  const querySnapshot = await getDocs(q);
  querySnapshot.forEach((doc) => {
    console.log(doc.id, ' => ', doc.data());
  });
}"},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"Important Rules and Limitations"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"While range filters are powerful, Firestore enforces specific architectural constraints to ensure optimal query performance:"},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Single-field constraint: In a single query, all range and inequality filters must be applied on the same field."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Ordering requirement: If you include an explicit orderBy clause in your query, the first orderBy must reference the same field that is filtered by the inequality."},{"order":17,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"Using range filters and inequality constraints allows you to narrow down dataset results effectively in Firebase Firestore. Always verify your query structure against Firestore indexing rules to prevent runtime index errors."}]
